 * This file is used to store environment variables for the development environment.
 * You can create a .env file in the root of your project and add your environment variables there.
 * For example:
 * 
 * NODE_ENV=development
 * PORT=8080
 * MONGO_DB_URL=mongodb://localhost:27017/mydatabase
 * 
 * Then you can access these variables in your code using process.env.VARIABLE_NAME
 * For example:
 * 
 * const port = process.env.PORT || 8888;
 * const mongoDbUrl = process.env.MONGO_DB_URL;
 * 
 * Make sure to add .env to your .gitignore file to avoid committing sensitive information to your repository.
